        "original_id": "a2389d8c-b207-584b-8190-130eebf896bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Even, Incubus\n- People: Ash Naylor, Matthew Cotter, Wally Kempton, Wally Meanie\n- Places: Australia, Calabasas, California\n- Roles: singer-songwriter-guitarist, drummer, bassist, backing vocalist\n- Albums: Less Is More, Come Again, A Different High, Free Kicks, Even, In Another Time\n\nFacts:\n- Even formed in March 1994.\n- Even is an Australian indie rock three-piece.\n- Ash Naylor fronts Even as singer-songwriter-guitarist.\n- Matthew Cotter plays drums in Even.\n- Wally Kempton, also known as Wally Meanie, plays bass guitar and provides backing vocals in Even.\n- Even played regularly on the live music scene and toured nationally and internationally.\n- Even released the studio album \"Less Is More\" on 10 June 1996.\n- Even released the studio album \"Come Again\" on 28 September 1998.\n- Even released the studio album \"A Different High\" on 14 May 2001.\n- Even released the studio album \"Free Kicks\" on 6 June 2004.\n- Even released the self-titled studio album \"Even\" on 29 March 2008.\n- Even released the studio album \"In Another Time\" on 9 December 2011.\n- Incubus is an American rock band from Calabasas, California.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
